A||N||4||fierofrek||Can you swap reflector with backlit gauges?||||1||
Z||000000||fierofrek||06-26-2001||07:08 AM||||I have an 88 coupe with reflector type gauges and am going to the bone yard today before sleep, and was wondering if I pick up some backlit gauges will they just plug in and work with no/little mods? THX. :P<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://members.tripod.com/fierofrek" TARGET=_blank>http://members.tripod.com/fierofrek</A> <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||fierofrek||06-26-2001||08:57 AM||||Somebody/anybody????||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tweek||06-26-2001||09:58 AM||||Im going out on a limb and saying yes... But make sure its for the same motor, and closest year possible. If it doesnt work for you, but it still functional im sure you could resell iton here..||||reg||1
Z||000003||kslish||06-26-2001||04:14 PM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierofrek:<BR><B>I have an 88 coupe with reflector type gauges and am going to the bone yard today before sleep, and was wondering if I pick up some backlit gauges will they just plug in and work with no/little mods? THX. :P<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The guages swap fine....I've put backlit GT guages in my 4 cyl coupe, the wiring harness for the center console guages is even present on all '86-'88 Fieros reguardless of the engine.  <P>However, if you have a 4 cylinder, you will have to mess around a little with the tachometer to get it to read right.  There is a capacitor near the top of the circuit board that tunes the reading of the tach to the engine.  If the capacitor isn't changed or replaced with one of a slightly larger value (I actually just wired another one in parallel, effectively increasing the capacitance) the 6 cyl tach (which is the only Fiero tach that was backlit) will read too low when attached to a 4 cyl.  Mine still reads around 500 rpm too low at speed, but I'll get around to fixing it once I find the right value to use (not too big of a priority at the moment)...I increased the capacitor by 1000pf but I think I should have went with a 2000pf jump.  I've actually seen people swap in variable capacitors so you can fine tune the tach for anything from a 4 to a V8.  <P>------------------<P>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR>See them at <A HREF="http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html</A> <BR>Western PA Fiero Club - <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by kslish (edited 06-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierofrek||06-26-2001||10:16 PM||||kewl, thanks for the replys guys. :P I picked one up just in the off chance that it does work with my motor. I saw the "pig tail" connector and assumed it was for the external center gauges. I picked up the full dash (headlight switch, dimmer, and defogger) for $15 US, is that a good deal? (by the way, all gauges work, they hooked it up to a V6 SE in the work bay to test it, I noticed though the the middle of the tach had lost it's color? sun fade maybe? THX again people.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
